      "source_text": "U.S. macro: June CPI came in notably softer than expected, with core CPI flat m/m vs consensus +0.2% and headline CPI down -0.4% m/m vs consensus -0.1%. Annualized core fell to +2.6% and headline eased to +3.5%, both now reaching some of the lowest levels since the start of the 2026. Europe markets: European equities gained (Stoxx 50 +0.2%) despite earlier losses amid a re-escalation of U.S.-Iran tensions and a closure of the Strait of Hormuz.",
